# Pass 26 — Production Readiness. DEPLOYMENT.md has always instructed
# `copy .env.example .env` for the frontend's root config, with a fallback comment for
# "if no .env.example exists at root, create .env manually" — but this file never
# actually existed; a real, live `.env` (with these same two values) was committed in
# its place instead. That's the wrong pattern to follow going forward, even though
# these specific values are non-secret (REACT_APP_* variables are baked into the public
# JS bundle at build time by Create React App and are never actually private) — the
# committed root `.env` has been removed from tracking in the same commit that adds
# this file, so the documented `copy .env.example .env` step actually works as written.
REACT_APP_API_BASE_URL_LOCAL=http://localhost:5050/api/v1
REACT_APP_API_BASE_URL_LIVE=https://api.EXAMPLE.COM/api/v1
